cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuroPest or its biological connectome models in your research, please cite the software and the underlying foundational studies as below."
title: "NeuroPest: Biologically Grounded Drosophila Connectome Desktop Simulation"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-06"
repository-code: "https://github.com/IrohAmca/NeuroPest"
url: "https://github.com/IrohAmca/NeuroPest"
license: "PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  NeuroPest is an interactive computational biology system running a Leaky
  Integrate-and-Fire (LIF) simulation of the adult fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster)
  whole-brain connectome from FlyWire (v783). It translates real-time sensory inputs
  (cursor kinematics or optical desktop screen capture) into biophysical Poisson spike
  trains across visual, antennal, and mechanosensory projection neurons, decoding motor
  behaviors directly from descending command neurons (Giant Fiber, MDN, DNp09, DNa02,
  aDN1/aDN2) and modeling associative reinforcement learning in the Mushroom Body.
keywords:
  - computational-neuroscience
  - drosophila-melanogaster
  - connectome
  - flywire
  - leaky-integrate-and-fire
  - descending-neurons
  - mushroom-body
  - reinforcement-learning
  - neuromorphic-simulation
